WEBVTT

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.520
Look, the sky up above has begun to move.
Hora miageta sora ugokidashita yo

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.750
Your astonishment was so dazzling.
Odoroku kimi mabushikute

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:27.810
Should I forgive the lies you told me yesterday
Kinou tsuita uso mo yurusou kana

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.090
just because the morning light is so pretty?
Kesa no hikari kirei dakara

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:38.170
The sound of your laughter is always important to me
Kimi no warai goe itsu datte daiji da yo

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:41.820
because it gives me courage.
Yuuki kureru kara saa

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.680
It's not a lie.
Uso ja nai

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.460
It's a beauty really
It's a beauty really

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.610
Your voice whenever.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.110
It makes me have.
Your voice whenever.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:50.920
It makes me have.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.660
Even the silliest things sound dear,
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:57.980
Sasai na koto mo itoshiku hibiku yo
Even the silliest things sound dear,

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:01.540
if it's your voice I hear.
kimi no koe nara

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:03.810
You're sad whenever.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.120
It takes you back.
You're sad whenever.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:05.480
It takes you back.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.840
My heart runneth over.
Hamidasu kokoro

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:16.070
Unable to control myself, I set off at a run.
Osaerarenakute hashiri dashita yo

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.050
I can forever.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.870
Well, I'd say it's all right.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:49.490
Just "all right"?

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:53.830
How can you call this wonderful script merely "all right"?

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.950
Is that the extent of your opinion?

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:57.380
Okay, okay, okay, okay.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:01.650
Toujou's done it again.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:04.600
We're definitely using this script for this year's contest submission.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.440
I agree too!

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:10.770
I'm glad.

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:13.560
But I don't know if Satsuki's right for this heroine...

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.580
Ah! Wonderful!

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.960
Toujou-san, did you have me in mind when you wrote this part?

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:21.470
This heroine is a perfect fit for me.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.820
Umm, well, yes and no...

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:27.070
Are you going to decide so quickly?

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.700
What are you saying?!

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.570
If I don't play this part, who <i>will?</i>

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:36.040
That's not the point. I'm only saying we haven't decided anything yet.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.550
Come now...

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.720
Satsuki-chan, sit down, have a seat.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:47.770
Reunion in the Rain

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:59.690
I was about to start
sleep-stripping again.

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.200
Still awake, Junpei?

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:08.160
What is that? 4-panel manga?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.710
Dang it, Yui. Don't scare me like that.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:15.900
It's 3 AM. If you keep drawing manga, you won't wake up in the morning.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:17.210
Shut up.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:21.530
Right now, I'm burning to show the greatness of Toujou's script

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:24.120
to even bigger audiences.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.260
And besides, this isn't
a 4-panel manga,

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.730
it's a very important
movie storyboard...

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:32.910
Aaannd you're already asleep!

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:37.850
Once you start talking about movies, you just don't stop. Good night.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:41.140
Seriously, did she only
wake up to interrupt me?

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.700
What we should do about the heroine?

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.710
Toujou-san is really talented, isn't she?

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.750
I cried a bit while I was reading it.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:01.400
Hey Manaka, let's make a good movie.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.720
Yeah, you're right.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.870
About that, I was thinking that you'd fit better

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:11.130
as the protagonist's childhood friend.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:16.020
Hey, Manaka, did you know that the class reps are meeting today?

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:21.740
Sotomura, Toujou-san and
Misuzu-chan are all class reps, so...

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.940
They'll be late to club today.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:29.530
Also, Komiyama said he had
something to do at home today.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:33.070
So for the time being, it's just us.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:37.530
T-Time out! Calm down, Satsuki.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.580
You... you know, Satsuki...

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.830
Why don't we call off
the club meeting today?

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:49.050
I-I haven't made any progress with the storyboards, either.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:54.210
So why don't we try rehearsing the climax of the movie?

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:58.060
Doesn't the protagonist confess to the heroine...

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:02.340
...saying "don't go!"?
Can we rehearse that part?

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:06.170
Erm, I haven't memorized
that scene yet.

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:07.940
Or even read it, for that matter.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.660
It's okay; I'll take the lead.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:13.200
See, like this...

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.120
She draws near to the protagonist.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.370
Thank you.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.040
I...

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:26.510
Th-There wasn't a kissing scene there--

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:31.570
I'm not the protagonist! And the heroine...

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:32.530
Who is it?

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:37.660
The heroine that you just
imagined wasn't me, right?

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.520
So who was it?

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.520
No, that's not it.

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:45.160
Just a bright, but sort of
mysterious and delicate...

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:50.480
Who is it? Come on and tell me.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:57.430
Ah! I-I think I'll go home.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:05:59.650
I still haven't finished the storyboards.

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:01.710
Y-Yes, good luck with them.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:03.920
B-Bye.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:04.880
Bye-bye.

00:06:05.150 --> 00:06:06.250
Hold it.

00:06:08.920 --> 00:06:10.720
W-What is it?

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.770
I just wanted to give this to you.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:23.260
"Theatre Izumizaka".
There was a theater by that name?

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.750
Apparently it'd been closed for a long time,

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:29.270
but its old owner recently started running it again as a hobby.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:33.240
Anyway, they play good movies there,
not mediocre tripe.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:35.920
Of course, they're all revivals of old movies.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:38.780
You're acting so kind it's scaring me.

00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:42.430
I just thought the movie they're
currently showing would give you

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:46.240
some ideas for impressing audiences with Toujou-san's script.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:50.190
Now that I've joined, I'd hate to be associated with a crappy movie.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.080
That's harsh.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:55.360
And as odd as you may be,
you <i>are</i> the director, right?

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.070
If you can't communicate what you want to say,

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.220
you'll never amount to anything.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:03.400
Would you really want to watch...

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:07.600
...a movie directed by someone who can't make up his mind?

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.070
You heard?

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:16.070
Yeah, you were practically yelling.

00:07:16.610 --> 00:07:19.840
Sheesh, what do you see in him?

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.490
I don't get it at all.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:23.130
But he's very kind.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:26.910
Sure, it'd be nice if he were only kind to <i>me</i>, but...

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.180
It's no use.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:31.920
Right now, I'm the furthest away from Manaka.

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:38.030
They say, "She who falls in love, loses at love."

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:39.950
And it seems like "they" were right.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:43.110
S-Shut up! You don't even know anything about love.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:45.890
I'm still aiming for
a comeback, you know.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.680
Fine, whatever.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.280
By the way, Kitaouji-senpai,

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:53.090
I really think you'd be perfect for the role of

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:55.440
the protagonist's childhood friend.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:57.440
I'm going to play the heroine!

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.820
Like I'm saying,
you aren't suited for it.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.790
I don't want to play another role.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:06.530
Manaka-kun!

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:09.210
Ah, Toujou...

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:12.420
I happened to come up
with a new idea.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.540
And I wanted to get your take on it.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:18.590
Manaka-kun?

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:21.200
I'm hopeless.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:22.500
What's wrong?

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:26.860
You've worked so hard to write such a good script, but...

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:31.230
With a director like me, I don't think the movie can ever be good.

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:35.440
Even though I said I want to make a good movie,

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:39.860
I can't even turn down Satsuki and recast the heroine role...

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:42.250
Just a minute ago, Misuzu said

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:46.750
that any movie I made wouldn't amount to anything.

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:51.630
Sorry, this isn't something I should be saying to you.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.380
I really am hopeless.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.510
Don't say that.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.880
I don't have that much
confidence either.

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.880
Truthfully, I think the reason why I'm
here right now, why I'm me right now,

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.150
is because you were there for me.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.800
Even just last year, you used
my script for the movie, right?

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:15.520
I've never told you this properly,
but I really thought you were amazing.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:19.140
And when I first
watched it, I cried a bit.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:23.570
That's why it'll be okay. Just believe in yourself.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:25.760
Let's make another wonderful movie.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:28.890
Thank you.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.250
Theatre Izumizaka

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:40.220
It was an old love story.
Theatre Izumizaka

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:43.080
But that love story...

00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.950
echoed painfully throughout my heart.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.940
Sir...

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.190
The movie's already over.

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:54.470
Are you going to watch it again on a free pass?

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:56.730
One can only be so impudent--

00:10:03.020 --> 00:10:06.800
I thought they only watched sci-fi
movies with CG animation,

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:10.310
but today's youngsters can still appreciate the classics.

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:12.160
Looks like I took them for granted.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:25.600
Can you please bring that potted plant inside?

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:26.600
Okay.

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:33.140
N-Nishino...

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:34.820
Junpei-kun...

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:42.260
I'm leaving now.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:45.450
Okay, good job today.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.710
Nishino, you were working at that cake shop?

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.910
Yup, the cakes at that shop are very delicious.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:55.120
Right now, it's just a part-time job.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.920
But if I keep at it, they'll let me help with the cooking someday.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:10:59.960
I see.

00:11:00.540 --> 00:11:04.210
Nishino is following her own path as usual.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.110
Hey, Junpei-kun?

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:08.470
What have you been doing after we broke up?

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:13.020
I went and watched a lot of movies.

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:19.090
The other day, I saw the love story movie at the theater by the cake shop.

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:23.020
And I was wondering if you saw it too.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.610
The movie I just saw...

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:30.400
It was an old movie,
but it was really entertaining.

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:32.280
I see.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:36.520
Nishino <i>had</i> said that she was
interested in making movies.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:39.460
But...

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.040
And when it was over, I cried.

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:46.390
Right now, that's impossible.

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.760
Well, my house is this way.

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:50.590
Yeah.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:51.880
Don't you need an umbrella?

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:54.150
I'm okay. The rain's letting up anyway.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:55.600
See ya.

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:57.020
Ah, okay.

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:02.440
Junpei-kun, are you
making another movie?

00:12:04.590 --> 00:12:05.450
Yeah.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:08.260
Show it to me when it's finished,  okay?

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:09.580
I will.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:10.940
I'm looking forward to it.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.560
[ Izumizaka Station North Gate ]

00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:39.400
I'll be back later this afternoon, okay?

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:41.350
No problem.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:49.700
That person... might just work.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:54.710
The True Heroine

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:07.260
You never once thought about my feelings, did you?

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.680
Hey Manaka, how was that reading?

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.050
It sounded good. You're great, Satsuki-chan!

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:13.800
Y-Yeah.

00:13:14.150 --> 00:13:16.340
Hey... listen properly, okay?

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:20.760
You never once thought about my feelings, did you?

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:32.500
Manaka.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:37.700
Cut! Cut! Cut! Cut!

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:39.780
Hey, Manaka~

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:43.220
Manaka? Hey... Are you
listening to me?

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.350
How was my acting just now?

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.040
Satsuki...

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:50.360
I really want you...

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:52.810
...to play the part of
the childhood friend.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:53.790
Eh?

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:57.730
Who do you have besides me to play the heroine? Toujou-san?

00:13:58.090 --> 00:13:59.820
No, that's not it.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:03.600
It's not like I have anybody specific in mind.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:06.540
Then what's the problem
with casting Satsuki-chan?

00:14:06.540 --> 00:14:08.390
That's not the issue.

00:14:08.390 --> 00:14:10.050
I really don't get it.

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:11.370
Wait just a second.

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:14.400
I've been pondering this, and...

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:20.370
What? We won't use Toujou's script?!

00:14:21.370 --> 00:14:23.080
Not that.

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.920
I'm saying we can't
film in this condition.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.370
So all we can do is
change the script, right?

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:31.740
It's not like there's a problem with the story Toujou created!

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:35.770
If we can't decide on a heroine, that means the script is plenty problematic.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.350
That's no reason to up and change the script!

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:41.270
Ah! Toujou-senpai...!?

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:58.000
T-Toujou was out there?

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:02.630
What happened? Toujou had an
incredibly shocked look on her face.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:06.280
The truth is...

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:11.380
Since we couldn't decide on a heroine,
I suggested a script rewrite.

00:15:11.380 --> 00:15:12.630
Stupid brother!

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:16.640
That's not Toujou's fault at all!
You imbecilic, moronic, idiotic cretin!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:17.060
Guidance Office

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:18.180
I'll go look for her!

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:19.400
Me too!

00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:20.060
Guidance Office

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.050
Me three!

00:15:21.050 --> 00:15:21.060
Guidance Office

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:33.120
I guess my script wasn't good enough...

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:38.790
Toujou!

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:46.330
M-Manaka-kun...

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:55.630
S-Sorry!

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:02.190
I'm reminded of that time back in middle school.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:05.540
Toujou cascading down with the sunset as a backdrop...

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:08.310
But if I had to name one difference,

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:11.100
it'd be that I didn't know Toujou back then.

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:14.900
And Toujou couldn't see me clearly without her glasses.

00:16:16.150 --> 00:16:17.620
Didn't something like this happen...

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:20.740
...on the roof during our 3rd year of middle school?

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:24.540
Toujou really knew it was me.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:28.450
I wonder if this is
some kind of an omen.

00:16:28.450 --> 00:16:30.920
That's twice you've seen me act so clumsy.

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:32.850
You remembered.

00:16:33.410 --> 00:16:36.320
I see. You knew it was me.

00:16:36.680 --> 00:16:37.350
Yeah.

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:43.560
I'm sorry my script was so bad...

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:47.440
What? Your script isn't bad at all.

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:49.560
But,

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:54.110
if we can't find a heroine, we can't make a movie.

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:59.690
I apologize. It's all because l came up with that kind of story.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:03.730
And now you and
Sotomura-kun are fighting.

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:09.540
I like the story that you wrote, Toujou.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.530
I want to film that script.

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:14.960
I <i>know</i> that we can do it.

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:18.730
All I can do is pour my heart into making a good movie out of it.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:22.800
I'll find a heroine if it's
the last thing I do.

00:17:26.070 --> 00:17:29.550
This is similar to what happened back in middle school, isn't it?

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.630
Hey, Manaka-kun,

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:35.350
would it be wrong of me
to think of it as fate?

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:37.080
Toujou...

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:42.880
Do you remember the time when we returned to that place?

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:49.080
I was obsessed with making a movie out of your novel.

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:50.840
Yeah... yeah...

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:52.500
Even now,

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:56.640
I'm thinking about how I might
make your story into a movie.

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:59.090
Like that last scene...

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:03.520
"We probably will never meet again."

00:18:04.020 --> 00:18:05.810
Yes, that scene.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:08.340
The protagonist was
calling out from inside a train.

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:11.570
Desperately trying
to raise the window.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.020
"That's why I won't forget."

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:16.650
"Your voice. Your eyes."

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:19.360
"The scenery we saw together."

00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:23.420
The prairie spread out on the other side of the train car.

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:29.000
And there, the heroine is running with a smile on her face.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.450
She's laughing.

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:36.010
"And the dazzling summer we spent together."

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:39.270
Her smile dissolves
into pure whiteness,

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:43.100
and at the end, you see
the clear blue sky.

00:18:43.100 --> 00:18:44.970
The blue sky of summer.

00:18:44.970 --> 00:18:47.240
See, it'll definitely work out.

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:49.220
Can't you see it, Toujou?

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:53.730
Yes, I can see it.

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:57.110
This is the only place left!

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.740
If anything goes wrong,
it'll be all <i>your</i> fault!

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:02.740
Toujou-san... Thank goodness...

00:19:03.080 --> 00:19:05.240
Hey now, what've you two been doing?

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.380
Hold it, Manaka.
What's that hand up to?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.050
Hey, listen!

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:14.390
This morning, I found someone
who'd be perfect as the heroine.

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:16.790
Why don't we all go and meet her now?

00:19:17.690 --> 00:19:19.420
I-Is it a beautiful girl?

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:26.470
Once you meet her, you won't even consider anyone else.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:28.430
Is she that cute of a girl?

00:19:28.920 --> 00:19:31.280
She's the only one I could think of.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:34.430
No matter who she is,
I'll thoroughly examine her.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:38.770
She's so passionate about this.
What sort of girl could she have found?

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:45.290
The only thing at the end of this street is... that store.

00:19:46.020 --> 00:19:47.370
We're here!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:51.910
I-I KNEW it!

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:54.920
Isn't this place a cake shop?

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:57.790
Actually, no one's here but the owner.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:02.300
How strange. She said she'd be here again today.

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:06.020
If it's for a pretty girl,
I'll wait forever.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:07.540
Yeah, me too.

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:10.510
Thank goodness. Nishino still hasn't gotten here.

00:20:10.510 --> 00:20:12.020
Manaka-kun, what's wrong?

00:20:12.020 --> 00:20:14.180
Ah, ahh, this is, umm...

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:15.800
You're drenched in sweat.

00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:18.170
What's wrong, Junpei-kun?

00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:20.080
Ah, nothing really.

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:22.490
I-It can't be that the heroine-- Nishi--!

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.070
Nishino-san!

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.910
Ni-Nishino Tsukasa-chan!

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:30.200
What is this? Do you guys know her?

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:30.910
Yeah.

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:34.420
What's going on? Did you all come to eat some cake?

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:42.160
I see... From the beginning,
the heroine...

00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:46.150
Come on in! We just got some new, highly-recommendable cakes!

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:49.300
Nishino!

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:01.030
Junpei-kun...

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:04.930
Nishino, we want you to appear in our movie.

00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:06.740
As the heroine.

00:21:08.090 --> 00:21:11.290
Didn't you say that you wanted to participate in the movie, Nishino?

00:21:12.070 --> 00:21:15.790
Please! The only one who can fill this part is you.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:18.720
Toujou-san?

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:22.800
Sure. I'm fine with you, Nishino-san.

00:21:28.530 --> 00:21:29.260
Sure.

00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:30.290
Way to go!

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:31.140
Can't breathe!
Way to go!

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:33.670
Thank you, Nishino-san.

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:34.600
Let's work together.

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:36.850
Manaka!

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:44.200
At that moment, all I could think about was the movie...

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:49.000
Go go!
